1. DEFINITIONS

   "SDK" means the CallerAPI software development kits published by CallerAPI,
   in any distributed form, including the iOS (Swift) package, the Android
   (Kotlin and native) library, the Flutter plugin, the React Native module,
   and their accompanying source code, binaries, templates, example projects,
   and documentation.

   "Service" means the CallerAPI backend (caller identification and spam-
   blocking data served via Private Information Retrieval and k-anonymous
   lookup at api.callerapi.com, pir.callerapi.com, pat.callerapi.com, or
   successor endpoints) that the SDK connects to.

   "Licensee" means the company or individual that has entered into a paid
   subscription agreement with CallerAPI to use the SDK and Service.

   "Application" means a Licensee's iOS or Android application that embeds the
   SDK.

   "Subscriber" means an end user of an Application for whom the Service
   performs lookups, as metered for billing under the subscription agreement.

